  "per_relation_cost_with_screen": "(1/P_SAT) * screen + s(l) * (1/P_SAT - 1) * 2^(alpha l) + 2^(alpha l)/recall; the last term (solving the SAT trial) is irreducible",
  "standard_operating_point_l_eq_n_over_m": "UNSAT trials per relation = m! - 1; maximal gain of a perfect free screen = m! (6x at m=3, 24x at m=4), a constant; the idea's formula C(ml+d0,d0)^omega + 2^((alpha-beta) l) omits the SAT solve",
  "undersized_base_optimum_with_perfect_screen": "l = n/(m+alpha), exponent (1+alpha)/(m+alpha); sub-rho iff alpha < m-2 (m=3: alpha<1; m=4: alpha<2) against measured alpha ~ m (idea: 4.1-4.3 at m=4): exponents 0.667 (m=3,alpha=3), 0.630-0.639 (m=4), all above 0.5",
